# OPUS-ROOT-CALL-20260930-17: the two-argument form written above Other's declaration.  The language (docs :668):
# Model exists, so `Model: Other extra` is Model's call -- an ordinary named Structure takes no argument -- whatever
# Other is: refused at the call by its arity, as with Other declared above (unit_root_struct_call2_refused).  K03
# NS-ROLES-CALL removed the old typed receiving route that took the line while Other was invisible (the implementation
# debt K03 NS-ROLES-VIS pinned here, Codex K03-VIS-CALL-CLASSIFICATION-20261007-16).
Model:
    size_t: value 1U
end: Model

int: extra 1
Model: Other extra

Other:
    size_t: p 2U
end: Other
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
